Unauthenticated users could access protected dashboard pages via AI chatbot links or direct URL navigation. The chatbot was showing dashboard options to guests, and client-side auth checks ran too late to prevent content flash.

## Changes

### chatbot.js
- Added `isAuthenticated()` check before determining user role
- `detectUserRole()` now returns `guest` for unauthenticated users regardless of URL
- `getRoleLinks()` returns login page for unauthenticated users
- Link interceptor redirects to login when clicking dashboard links without session

### page-access-token.js
- Added `hidePageContent()`/`showPageContent()` to prevent content flash during auth check
- Enhanced `initPageAccessGuard()` with immediate content hiding and role-based access validation

### All 25 dashboard pages
- Added inline auth script in `<head>` that executes before any content loads:

```html
<script>
    (function() {
        'use strict';
        function checkAuth() {
            try {
                var accessToken = localStorage.getItem('accessToken');
                var user = localStorage.getItem('user');
                if (!accessToken || !user) return false;
                var userData = JSON.parse(user);
                return userData && userData.role === 'student'; // role varies per page
            } catch (e) { return false; }
        }
        if (!checkAuth()) {
            sessionStorage.setItem('loginRedirect', window.location.pathname);
            window.location.replace('/login.html');
            document.write('<html><body><p>Redirecting...</p></body></html>'); return;
        }
    })();
</script>
```

Each page validates the user has the correct role (student/teacher/admin) for that specific dashboard.

